    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "https://www.auctioneera.ie/property/10-kinvara-close-ballyvolane-cork-t23-x88a-1\r\nImportant note: Details of upcoming viewings and latest offers are available at the Auctioneera website link above.\r\n\r\nAuctioneera is delighted to present 10 Kinvara Close, Ballyvolane.\r\n\r\nNestled within the inviting community of Ballyvolane, Cork, this property presents a charming semi-detached home, ideal for those seeking a blend of comfort and convenience. The exterior of this property is framed by a small, mature front garden, adorned with shrubs, small trees, and decorative pot plants, adding a welcoming touch to the façade. The well-maintained garden path leads to the main entrance, offering both visual appeal and practicality.\r\n\r\nInside, the property opens into a bright and airy living space designed for modern living. The ground floor hosts a spacious lounge with ample natural light, perfect for relaxing or entertaining guests. Adjacent to the lounge, the kitchen is fitted with contemporary units and provides sufficient space for dining, making it an ideal spot for family meals. Conveniently, this level also features a small toilet and wash hand basin, adding to the practicality of the layout.\r\n\r\nThe upper floor comprises three well-proportioned bedrooms, each offering comfortable accommodation. The main bedroom boasts an en suite, fully tiled for ease of maintenance and featuring a shower and toilet, ensuring privacy and convenience for its occupants. Two additional bedrooms offer flexible living spaces suitable for family members or guests.\r\n\r\nA particular highlight of this property is the generous rear garden. Enhanced by a large slabbed patio, it provides an excellent area for outdoor dining and seasonal activities. The garden is completed by a 24-square-metre steeltech shed, equipped with electricity and perspex panels for daylight.\r\n\r\nKinvara Close benefits from proximity to various local amenities, including schools, shops, and leisure facilities, alongside efficient transport links to Cork city centre. This home presents an attractive opportunity for first-time buyers or families seeking a conveniently located, well-maintained residence with ample outdoor space and modern comforts."
